Below is a sample rubric for the performance review of a software engineer, formatted in JSON. This rubric assesses various aspects of a software engineer's performance, including technical skills, collaboration, problem-solving, communication, adaptability, and overall impact on the team and organization.

```json
{
  "Performance Review Rubric for Software Engineer": {
    "Technical Skills": {
      "Description": "Assesses the engineer's proficiency in programming languages, software development methodologies, and tools relevant to the role.",
      "Criteria": [
        {
          "Excellent": "Demonstrates mastery of relevant programming languages and technologies. Consistently delivers high-quality, efficient, and well-documented code.",
          "Good": "Shows a strong understanding of relevant programming languages and technologies. Generally delivers good quality code, with some room for improvement in efficiency or documentation.",
          "Needs Improvement": "Displays a basic understanding of relevant programming languages and technologies but often requires guidance. Code quality is inconsistent, with significant room for improvement in efficiency and documentation.",
          "Unsatisfactory": "Lacks understanding of relevant programming languages and technologies. Fails to deliver acceptable code quality, impacting project timelines and quality."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Collaboration and Teamwork": {
      "Description": "Evaluates the engineer's ability to work effectively with the team, including communication, active listening, and contributing to a positive team culture.",
      "Criteria": [
        {
          "Excellent": "Consistently demonstrates excellent teamwork and collaboration skills. Actively contributes to team discussions, listens effectively, and supports colleagues.",
          "Good": "Generally shows good teamwork and collaboration skills. Contributes to team discussions and supports colleagues, with occasional room for improvement in active listening or initiative.",
          "Needs Improvement": "Displays some teamwork and collaboration skills but often requires encouragement to participate fully in team discussions and support colleagues.",
          "Unsatisfactory": "Frequently fails to demonstrate teamwork and collaboration skills, impacting team morale and project success."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Problem-Solving and Innovation": {
      "Description": "Assesses the engineer's ability to analyze problems, design solutions, and implement them effectively.",
      "Criteria": [
        {
          "Excellent": "Consistently demonstrates exceptional problem-solving skills, identifying innovative solutions that significantly impact project success.",
          "Good": "Generally shows good problem-solving skills, identifying effective solutions with some room for innovation.",
          "Needs Improvement": "Displays basic problem-solving skills but often requires guidance to identify effective solutions.",
          "Unsatisfactory": "Fails to demonstrate adequate problem-solving skills, frequently requiring significant guidance and impacting project timelines."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Communication": {
      "Description": "Evaluates the engineer's ability to clearly articulate ideas, plans, and results to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.",
      "Criteria": [
        {
          "Excellent": "Consistently communicates clearly and effectively with all stakeholders, tailoring communication style as needed.",
          "Good": "Generally communicates effectively with most stakeholders, with some room for improvement in clarity or adaptability.",
          "Needs Improvement": "Displays some communication skills but often struggles to articulate ideas clearly to all stakeholders.",
          "Unsatisfactory": "Frequently fails to communicate effectively, leading to misunderstandings and project delays."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Adaptability and Continuous Learning": {
      "Description": "Assesses the engineer's willingness to adapt to new technologies, processes, and priorities, and their commitment to ongoing learning.",
      "Criteria": [
        {
          "Excellent": "Consistently demonstrates a strong willingness to adapt to change and prioritize learning, seeking out new challenges and opportunities.",
          "Good": "Generally shows a positive attitude towards change and learning, with some room for improvement in proactively seeking new challenges.",
          "Needs Improvement": "Displays some adaptability and interest in learning but often requires encouragement to embrace change or seek new knowledge.",
          "Unsatisfactory": "Frequently resists change and shows little interest in learning new technologies or processes, impacting personal and team performance."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Overall Impact": {
      "Description": "Evaluates the engineer's overall contribution to the team and organization, including the quality of work, timeliness, and impact on project success.",
      "Criteria": [
        {
          "Excellent": "Consistently delivers high-quality work on time, significantly contributing to project success and positively impacting the team and organization.",
          "Good": "Generally delivers good quality work on time, contributing to project success with some room for improvement in quality or timeliness.",
          "Needs Improvement": "Delivers acceptable work but often requires guidance to meet quality or timeliness expectations, with some impact on project success.",
          "Unsatisfactory": "Frequently fails to deliver acceptable work, significantly impacting project timelines and success."
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

This rubric provides a comprehensive framework for evaluating a software engineer's performance across key areas. It's designed to be flexible and can be adjusted based on the specific needs and goals of the team or organization.
